WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.659 --> 00:00:04.760
Mortal Engines aimed to be a franchise-starting
epic, but it looks like the grandest thing

00:00:04.760 --> 00:00:06.720
about it is the scale of its failure.

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:10.660
Here's how this hundred-million dollar book
adaptation turned into one of the biggest

00:00:10.660 --> 00:00:12.840
box office bombs of 2018.

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:18.930
Mortal Engines is based on the 2001 book of
the same name by Philip Reeve, which launched

00:00:18.930 --> 00:00:21.660
a seven-book series of sequels and prequels.

00:00:21.890 --> 00:00:25.780
The post-apocalyptic story is based around
the premise of cities that are constantly

00:00:25.780 --> 00:00:29.840
in motion, roaming the world in competition
with each other over resources.

00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:35.010
The protagonist is a woman named Hester, who
wears a mask to hide scars she received from

00:00:35.010 --> 00:00:38.960
a man named Thaddeus, an evil historian in
London who killed her mother.

00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:43.480
To help get her vengeance on Thaddeus, Hester
joins up with a team of rebels who are fighting

00:00:43.480 --> 00:00:47.590
to make cities stop preying on each other,
and go back to sitting still.

00:00:47.590 --> 00:00:49.320
And that's honestly only the half of it.

00:00:49.560 --> 00:00:51.960
As you might imagine, there's a lot going
on here.

00:00:52.100 --> 00:00:54.120
"Just give it to me one more time, simpler."

00:00:55.100 --> 00:01:00.880
Over the course of its debut weekend, Mortal
Engines made only $7.5 million at the domestic

00:01:00.890 --> 00:01:05.770
box office, a crushingly low number that saw
the movie opening in fifth place.

00:01:05.770 --> 00:01:10.680
The film fared better in foreign markets,
where it brought in nearly $35 million, with

00:01:10.680 --> 00:01:15.220
the combined total making for an opening weekend
take of just over $42 million.

00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:19.260
Relative to the movie's budget, that's an
especially dismal performance.

00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:24.330
The production budget for Mortal Engines has
been reported as being over $100 million,

00:01:24.330 --> 00:01:28.740
with the marketing budget reportedly being
$120 million, according to Deadline.

00:01:28.980 --> 00:01:34.760
That means it may have cost in the realm of
$220 million to make and market Mortal Engines.

00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:38.420
With such a lousy opening weekend, the movie
is pretty much doomed.

00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:43.920
According to Deadline and other outlets, it
may well end up losing over $150 million by

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:45.240
the time its run is through.

00:01:46.120 --> 00:01:49.940
Mortal Engines had the misfortune of debuting
during a crowded time of year.

00:01:50.160 --> 00:01:54.260
On its debut weekend, it faced off against
Sony's Spider-Man: Into the Spider-Verse,

00:01:54.260 --> 00:01:58.160
an animated superhero feature that topped
the domestic box office.

00:01:58.380 --> 00:02:02.230
It also faced surprising competition from
Clint Eastwood's The Mule, which came out

00:02:02.230 --> 00:02:05.410
to one of the best financial performances
of the director's career.

00:02:05.410 --> 00:02:06.820
And those are just the brand-new movies.

00:02:06.900 --> 00:02:11.180
Audiences also spent the weekend with family
films like The Grinch or the Wreck-It Ralph

00:02:11.180 --> 00:02:13.980
sequel, still holding strong after several
weeks in theaters.

00:02:14.380 --> 00:02:18.700
Other big movies audiences are still catching
up on include Creed II, Bohemian Rhapsody,

00:02:18.700 --> 00:02:24.420
and the Fantastic Beasts sequel, with Once
Upon a Deadpool - the re-edited, PG-13 version

00:02:24.420 --> 00:02:28.500
of Deadpool 2 - also peeling away a few million
dollars worth of viewers for itself.

00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:34.640
"You dropped a super duber dumperuski in your
little diapey wipey, didn't you, buddy?"

00:02:34.700 --> 00:02:35.740
"Yes I did."

00:02:37.520 --> 00:02:41.560
Basically, there's no shortage of decent movies
to choose from in winter 2018.

00:02:41.560 --> 00:02:45.280
While Mortal Engines may have distinguished
itself from the rest of the pack with its

00:02:45.280 --> 00:02:49.220
weird premise, it totally failed to get people
interested in actually seeing it.

00:02:49.900 --> 00:02:53.680
A movie doesn't need great reviews to be a
success at the box office.

00:02:53.680 --> 00:02:57.080
But Mortal Engines proved a turn-off to audiences
and critics both.

00:02:57.660 --> 00:02:59.440
"That must've been one lousy movie."

00:02:59.640 --> 00:03:04.920
After its opening weekend, Mortal Engines
sat at a mere 28% on Rotten Tomatoes, with

00:03:04.920 --> 00:03:08.420
129 reviews being counted toward the movie's
average score.

00:03:08.420 --> 00:03:13.760
Writers referred to the movie as being wearying,
crummy, and a giant slog, with even the more

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:16.540
positive reviews typically finding something
to complain about.

00:03:16.950 --> 00:03:21.180
While some gave credit to the movie's special
effects, it seemed the movie's story failed

00:03:21.180 --> 00:03:22.560
to justify the spectacle.

00:03:22.740 --> 00:03:28.160
Compare this reception to a movie like Spider-Verse,
which is a recognizable franchise movie getting

00:03:28.170 --> 00:03:29.459
universal acclaim.

00:03:29.460 --> 00:03:33.260
Next to offerings like that, Mortal Engines
just looks like too much of a risk.

00:03:33.720 --> 00:03:37.800
Mortal Engines' biggest problem may be that
it's too difficult to advertise.

00:03:37.819 --> 00:03:42.930
The cities-on-wheels idea is just too high-concept,
and wasn't explained in a compelling way by

00:03:42.930 --> 00:03:43.860
the movie's marketing.

00:03:44.190 --> 00:03:48.320
This is less of a problem for a book series,
which gets time to build a world over many

00:03:48.320 --> 00:03:48.820
pages.

00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:54.020
But movies have to sell themselves with intriguing
posters, killer trailers, and concepts that

00:03:54.020 --> 00:03:55.710
could fit in a single sentence.

00:03:55.710 --> 00:03:59.080
For a story that's this out there, that's
a pretty tricky proposition.

00:03:59.260 --> 00:04:03.720
Complicating things is the fact that the book
series Mortal Engines is based on is relatively

00:04:03.720 --> 00:04:08.500
unpopular in the United States, compared to
series like The Hunger Games or Harry Potter.

00:04:08.500 --> 00:04:12.140
So Mortal Engines largely had to sell itself
on its merits as a movie.

00:04:12.460 --> 00:04:14.080
It apparently made for a hard sell.

00:04:14.270 --> 00:04:18.440
Imagining cities on wheels in a book is one
thing, but when you see them chasing each

00:04:18.440 --> 00:04:22.490
other across the landscape in a movie trailer,
it's easy to just be confused.

00:04:23.490 --> 00:04:27.640
Mortal Engines was produced in part by Peter
Jackson and Fran Walsh, with a screenplay

00:04:27.640 --> 00:04:30.180
by Jackson, Walsh, and Philippa Boyens.

00:04:30.770 --> 00:04:34.360
They're a creative team that rang in the new
millennium with their adaptations of The Lord

00:04:34.370 --> 00:04:39.520
of the Rings, making a stone-cold classic
trilogy of movies that remain the gold standard

00:04:39.520 --> 00:04:41.020
for epic book adaptations.

00:04:41.340 --> 00:04:45.419
But whatever magic helped to elevate those
films to Oscar-sweeping greatness failed to

00:04:45.419 --> 00:04:49.650
come into being with Mortal Engines, with
the property simply failing to generate enough

00:04:49.650 --> 00:04:50.820
interest among audiences.

00:04:51.320 --> 00:04:55.820
One reason why the movie failed is lousy timing
when it comes to cinematic trends.

00:04:55.830 --> 00:04:59.990
Jackson originally purchased the rights to
the Mortal Engines story over a decade ago,

00:04:59.990 --> 00:05:03.050
when adaptations of young adult novels were
more in fashion.

00:05:03.050 --> 00:05:07.880
Now the landscape is much different, and audiences
apparently aren't as attracted to these stories

00:05:07.880 --> 00:05:08.720
as they used to be.

00:05:08.950 --> 00:05:14.160
The Darkest Minds, another YA adaptation released
in August 2018, also proved a flop on its

00:05:14.169 --> 00:05:15.169
opening weekend.

00:05:15.169 --> 00:05:18.860
But that movie had a much smaller budget,
so its failure caused less damage.

00:05:19.120 --> 00:05:21.440
Mortal Engines was a big bet that didn't pay
off.

00:05:21.800 --> 00:05:25.620
Whether the filmmakers thought people would
come out for the property, or for Peter Jackson,

00:05:25.620 --> 00:05:26.620
they were wrong.

00:05:26.620 --> 00:05:28.100
Nobody wanted to see it at all.

00:05:28.100 --> 00:05:32.570
It was supposed to be a franchise-starter,
but instead it's ended up a fascinating failure.

